{{! Glimmer-header (Discourse 3.3+) connector. The new header replaced the
    widget "home-logo" outlet with a "home-logo-wrapper" WRAPPER outlet, and
    wrapper outlets are NOT extended by a plain connector + yield. Their content
    goes into the synthetic "name__before" / "name__after" outlets (what
    api.renderBeforeWrapperOutlet / renderAfterWrapperOutlet target). So this
    connector lives at "connectors/home-logo-wrapper__after/", rendering the
    SupportHub header right after the logo inside the (flex:1) wrapper. The
    legacy "connectors/home-logo/supporthub.hbs" still covers older
    (widget-header) Discourse, so both generations are supported. }}
{{#if siteSettings.supporthub_header_enabled}}
  <div class="supporthub-plugin">
    {{{site.supporthub_header_html}}}
  </div>
{{/if}}
